#!/bin/sh
# Drush 13+ requires a site-local install (vendor/bin/drush); a global Drush can
# no longer bootstrap a Drupal site. This shim does not run Drush at all, it only
# prints how to install and call the project-local Drush.
cat >&2 <<'EOF'
drush is not installed globally in this image.

Drush 13+ must be installed in your Drupal project and called from there:

  1) Install Drush once in the project:
       cd /var/www/html
       composer require drush/drush

  2) Call the project-local Drush directly:
       vendor/bin/drush status

  3) Or add the project's vendor/bin to PATH for the current shell:
       cd /var/www/html
       export PATH="$PWD/vendor/bin:$PATH"
       drush status

The PATH change only applies to the current shell session; run it again in every
new shell (or keep calling vendor/bin/drush directly).
EOF
exit 127
